window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-8848c931089e4021"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"create-a-cli-codex-can-use\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex\">创建 Codex 可用的命令行工具</h1> <p>为 API、日志来源、导出数据或团队脚本提供可组合的命令。</p> <p>请 Codex 创建一个可从任意目录运行的命令行工具；它可以与仓库脚本配合、下载文件，并通过配套技能让 Codex 记住如何使用。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>Codex 需要反复搜索、读取、下载或安全写入同一个服务、导出文件、本地归档或仓库脚本时。</li> <li>智能体工具需要分页搜索、按 ID 精确读取、可预测的 JSON、下载文件、本地索引，或“先起草再写入”的命令时。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/cli-creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$cli-creator（需联网）</a></td> <td>设计命令界面、构建 CLI、加入安装与身份验证检查、将命令安装到 PATH，并从另一个目录验证它。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.system/skill-creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$skill-creator（需联网）</a></td> <td>创建配套技能，说明后续 Codex 任务应先运行哪些 CLI 命令，以及哪些写入操作需要批准。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>构建 CLI 和配套技能</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $cli-creator 创建一个可供你使用的 CLI，并在同一聊天中使用 $skill-creator 创建配套技能。\n\n可供学习的来源（可按需替换或删减方括号中的示例）：[docs URL, OpenAPI spec, redacted curl command, existing script path, log folder, CSV or JSON export, SQLite database path, or pasted --help output]。\n\nCLI 首先应支持的任务（可按需选择或替换方括号中的示例）：[download failed CI logs from a build URL, search support tickets and read one by ID, query an admin API, read a local database, or run one step from an existing script]。\n\n可选的写入任务（可按需选择或替换方括号中的示例）：[create a draft comment, upload media, retry a failed job, or read-only for now]。\n\n命令名称：[cli-name, or recommend one]（填写命令名称，或请 Codex 推荐）。\n\n编写代码前，请先展示拟议的命令界面；只询问那些缺失且会阻碍构建的信息。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">技能</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23?anchor=create-a-skill\">创建自定义技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">简介</h2> <p>如果 Codex 经常要使用同一个 API、日志来源、导出收件箱、本地数据库或团队脚本，就为这类工作提供一个可组合的界面：让它能够从任意目录运行命令、检查结果、缩小范围，并把命令与 <code>git</code>、<code>gh</code>、<code>rg</code>、测试及仓库脚本组合起来。</p> <p>再创建一个配套技能，记录 Codex 何时应使用该 CLI、首先运行什么、如何控制输出大小、下载文件应保存在哪里，以及哪些写入命令需要批准。</p> <p>在这个工作流中，<code>$cli-creator</code> 帮 Codex 构建命令；<code>$skill-creator</code> 帮 Codex 保存可复用的技能，例如 <code>$ci-logs</code>，供未来任务按名称调用。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">使用方法</h2> <ol> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8848c931089e4021?anchor=choose-what-the-cli-should-do\">确定 CLI 应完成什么</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8848c931089e4021?anchor=share-the-docs-files-or-commands\">提供 Codex 应学习的来源</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8848c931089e4021?anchor=ask-codex-to-build-the-cli-and-skill\">运行 <code>$cli-creator</code></a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8848c931089e4021?anchor=verify-the-command-works-from-any-folder\">测试安装后的命令</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8848c931089e4021?anchor=use-the-skill-later\">稍后调用已保存的技能</a></li> </ol> <p><a id=\"choose-what-the-cli-should-do\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"cli\">确定 CLI 应完成什么</h2> <p>从你希望 Codex 完成的事情出发，而不是从希望它编写的技术出发。好的 CLI 会把重复的读取、搜索、下载、导出、起草、上传、轮询或安全写入，变成 Codex 可以从任意仓库运行的命令。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>情况</th> <th>Codex 可以用 CLI 做什么</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>CI 日志藏在构建页面后面。</strong></td> <td>接收构建 URL，把失败任务的日志下载到 <code>./logs</code>，并返回文件路径和简短片段。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>支持工单以每周导出文件的形式到达。</strong></td> <td>为最新的 CSV 或 JSON 导出文件建立索引，按客户或短语搜索，并按稳定 ID 读取单个工单。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>API 响应对上下文来说太大。</strong></td> <td>只列出所需字段，按 ID 读取完整对象，并把完整响应导出到文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Slack 导出包含很长的讨论串。</strong></td> <td>使用 <code>--limit</code> 搜索、读取单个讨论串，并返回附近的上下文，而不是整个归档。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>团队脚本要运行四个不同步骤。</strong></td> <td>将设置、发现、下载、起草、上传、轮询和实时写入拆分成独立命令。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>插件找到了记录，但 Codex 还需要一个文件。</strong></td> <td>在聊天中保留插件；用 CLI 下载附件、跟踪记录、报告、视频或日志包，并返回文件路径。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"share-the-docs-files-or-commands\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">提供文档、文件或命令</h2> <p>Codex 需要具体材料作为学习来源：文档或 OpenAPI、脱敏的 curl 命令、导出文件或数据库路径、日志目录，或现有脚本。如果希望 CLI 遵循熟悉的风格，可以粘贴 <code>gh</code>、<code>kubectl</code> 或团队自有工具的简短 <code>--help</code> 输出。</p> <p>如果命令需要身份验证，请告诉 Codex 它应支持的环境变量名称、配置文件路径或登录流程。请你自己在 shell 或配置文件中设置密钥，不要把密钥粘贴到聊天中。还可以要求 Codex 在缺少身份验证信息时，让 CLI 的设置检查明确失败。</p> <p><a id=\"ask-codex-to-build-the-cli-and-skill\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-cli\">请 Codex 构建 CLI 和技能</h2> <p>使用本页的起步提示词，填写 Codex 应学习的来源，以及 CLI 首先应支持的任务。</p> <p>Codex 写代码之前，应先展示拟议的命令界面；只询问那些缺失且会阻碍构建的信息。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-the-command-works-from-any-folder\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">验证命令能从任意目录运行</h2> <p>不要让 Codex 在运行 <code>cargo run</code>、<code>python path/to/script.py</code> 或未安装的软件包命令后就停止。请它在另一个仓库或临时文件夹中测试安装后的命令，模拟未来任务的实际用法。</p> <p><strong>像未来的智能体一样测试 CLI</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Test [cli-name] the way you would use it in a future task.\n\nPlease show proof that:\n\n- command -v [cli-name] succeeds from outside the CLI source folder\n- [cli-name] --help explains the main commands\n- the setup/auth check runs\n- one safe discovery, list, or search command works\n- one exact read command works with an ID from the discovery result\n- any large log, export, trace, or payload writes to a file and returns the path\n- live write commands are not run unless I explicitly approved them\n\nThen read the companion skill and tell me the shortest prompt I should use when I need this CLI again.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请按照未来任务中的实际用法测试 [cli-name]。\n\n请展示证据，证明：\n\n- 在 CLI 源码目录之外运行 command -v [cli-name] 能够成功\n- [cli-name] --help 能解释主要命令\n- 能够运行配置或身份验证检查\n- 一条安全的发现、列举或搜索命令能够正常工作\n- 能够使用发现结果中的 ID，运行一条精确读取命令\n- 任何大型日志、导出、追踪记录或载荷都会写入文件并返回路径\n- 除非我明确批准，否则不会运行实际写入命令\n\n然后阅读配套技能，并告诉我下次需要使用这个 CLI 时，应该输入的最简短提示词。</div></div> <p>如果 Codex 返回一大段 JSON，可以要求它缩小默认响应范围，并为完整载荷增加文件导出。如果它忘了审批边界，请先要求它更新配套技能，再在另一项任务中使用。</p> <p><a id=\"use-the-skill-later\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">稍后使用技能</h2> <p>需要再次使用 CLI 时，调用技能即可，不必重新粘贴文档。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $ci-logs to download the failed logs for this build URL and tell me the first failing step.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请使用 $ci-logs 下载这个构建 URL 对应的失败日志，并告诉我第一个失败的步骤。</div></div> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $support-export to search this week's refund complaints and read the three highest-value tickets.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请使用 $support-export 搜索本周关于退款的投诉，并阅读价值最高的三张工单。</div></div> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $admin-api to find this user's workspace, read the billing record, and draft a safe account note.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请使用 $admin-api 查找这名用户的工作区，读取账单记录，并起草一条安全妥当的账户备注。</div></div> <p>如果要定期执行，请先在一次聊天中测试该技能，再要求 Codex <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">为同一调用安排计划任务</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"create-a-cli-codex-can-use\">Create a CLI Codex can use</h1> <p>Give Codex a composable command for an API, log source, export, or team script.</p> <p>Ask Codex to create a composable CLI it can run from any folder, combine with repo scripts, use to download files, and remember through a companion skill.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Repeated work where Codex needs to search, read, download from, or safely write to the same service, export, local archive, or repo script.</li> <li>Agent tools that need paged search, exact reads by ID, predictable JSON, downloaded files, local indexes, or draft-before-write commands.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/cli-creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$cli-creator (online)</a></td> <td>Design the command surface, build the CLI, add setup and auth checks, install the command on PATH, and verify it from another folder.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.system/skill-creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$skill-creator (online)</a></td> <td>Create the companion skill that teaches later Codex tasks which CLI commands to run first and which write actions require approval.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build a CLI and companion skill</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $cli-creator to create a CLI you can use, and use $skill-creator to create the companion skill in this same chat.\n\nSource to learn from: [docs URL, OpenAPI spec, redacted curl command, existing script path, log folder, CSV or JSON export, SQLite database path, or pasted --help output].\n\nFirst job the CLI should support: [download failed CI logs from a build URL, search support tickets and read one by ID, query an admin API, read a local database, or run one step from an existing script].\n\nOptional write job: [create a draft comment, upload media, retry a failed job, or read-only for now].\n\nCommand name: [cli-name, or recommend one].\n\nBefore coding, show me the proposed command surface and ask only for missing details that would block the build.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Skills</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23?anchor=create-a-skill\">Create custom skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>When Codex keeps using the same API, log source, exported inbox, local database, or team script, give that work a composable interface: a command it can run from any folder, inspect, narrow, and combine with <code>git</code>, <code>gh</code>, <code>rg</code>, tests, and repo scripts.</p> <p>Add a companion skill that records when Codex should use the CLI, what to run first, how to keep output small, where downloaded files land, and which write commands need approval.</p> <p>In this workflow, <code>$cli-creator</code> helps Codex build the command. <code>$skill-creator</code> helps Codex save a reusable skill such as <code>$ci-logs</code>, which future tasks can invoke by name.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <ol> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8848c931089e4021?anchor=choose-what-the-cli-should-do\">Decide whether the job needs a CLI</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8848c931089e4021?anchor=share-the-docs-files-or-commands\">Share the source Codex should learn from</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8848c931089e4021?anchor=ask-codex-to-build-the-cli-and-skill\">Run <code>$cli-creator</code></a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8848c931089e4021?anchor=verify-the-command-works-from-any-folder\">Test the installed command</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8848c931089e4021?anchor=use-the-skill-later\">Invoke the saved skill later</a></li> </ol> <h2 id=\"choose-what-the-cli-should-do\">Choose what the CLI should do</h2> <p>Start with the thing you want Codex to do, not the technology you want it to write. A good CLI turns a repeated read, search, download, export, draft, upload, poll, or safe write into a command Codex can run from any repo.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Situation</th> <th>What Codex can do with the CLI</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>CI logs live behind a build page.</strong></td> <td>Take a build URL, download failed job logs to <code>./logs</code>, and return file paths plus short snippets.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Support tickets arrive as a weekly export.</strong></td> <td>Index the newest CSV or JSON export, search by customer or phrase, and read one ticket by stable ID.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>An API response is too large for context.</strong></td> <td>List only the fields it needs, read the full object by ID, and export the complete response to a file.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>A Slack export has long threads.</strong></td> <td>Search with <code>--limit</code>, read one thread, and return nearby context instead of the whole archive.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>A team script runs four different steps.</strong></td> <td>Split setup, discovery, download, draft, upload, poll, and live write into separate commands.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>A plugin finds the record, but Codex needs a file.</strong></td> <td>Keep the plugin in the chat; use a CLI to download the attachment, trace, report, video, or log bundle and return the path.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"share-the-docs-files-or-commands\">Share the docs, files, or commands</h2> <p>Codex needs something concrete to learn from: docs or OpenAPI, a redacted curl command, an export or database path, a log folder, or an existing script. If you want the CLI to follow a familiar style, paste a short <code>--help</code> output from <code>gh</code>, <code>kubectl</code>, or your team's own tool.</p> <p>If the command needs auth, tell Codex the environment variable name, config file path, or login flow it should support. Set the secret yourself in your shell or config file. Do not paste secrets into the chat. Ask Codex to make the CLI's setup check fail clearly when auth is missing.</p> <h2 id=\"ask-codex-to-build-the-cli-and-skill\">Ask Codex to build the CLI and skill</h2> <p>Use the starter prompt on this page. Fill in the source Codex should learn from and the first job the CLI should support.</p> <p>Before Codex writes code, it should show the proposed command surface and ask only for missing details that would block the build.</p> <h2 id=\"verify-the-command-works-from-any-folder\">Verify the command works from any folder</h2> <p>Codex should not stop after <code>cargo run</code>, <code>python path/to/script.py</code>, or an uninstalled package command. Ask it to test the installed command from another repo or a temporary folder, the way a later task will use it.</p> <p><strong>Test the CLI like a future agent</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Test [cli-name] the way you would use it in a future task.\n\nPlease show proof that:\n\n- command -v [cli-name] succeeds from outside the CLI source folder\n- [cli-name] --help explains the main commands\n- the setup/auth check runs\n- one safe discovery, list, or search command works\n- one exact read command works with an ID from the discovery result\n- any large log, export, trace, or payload writes to a file and returns the path\n- live write commands are not run unless I explicitly approved them\n\nThen read the companion skill and tell me the shortest prompt I should use when I need this CLI again.\n</code></pre> <p>If Codex returns a giant JSON blob, ask it to narrow the default response and add a file export for full payloads. If it forgets the approval boundary, ask it to update the companion skill before you use it in another task.</p> <h2 id=\"use-the-skill-later\">Use the skill later</h2> <p>When you need the CLI again, invoke the skill instead of pasting the docs again:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $ci-logs to download the failed logs for this build URL and tell me the first failing step.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $support-export to search this week's refund complaints and read the three highest-value tickets.\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $admin-api to find this user's workspace, read the billing record, and draft a safe account note.\n</code></pre> <p>For recurring work, test the skill once in a chat, then ask Codex to <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">schedule a task for that same invocation from the chat</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p>"};
